# P9-002: pfile writers — implementation plan

The actionable, phased build plan for the writers. **Decisions live in
`P9-001-writers-design`** (feasibility confirmed by two spikes); this doc is the
"how/steps." Target: everything ships together as **v0.8.x**.

## Status

- [ ] Phase A — CopyFunction scaffold + `.pvar`/`.psam` text writers (no pgenlib)
- [ ] Phase B — `.pgen` writer (pgenlib; hardcalls → phase → dosage)
- [ ] Phase C — `pfile` bundle (one COPY fans out all three)
- [ ] Phase D — partitioned (sharded) output wrapper
- [ ] Phase E — PLINK-VCF writer
- [ ] Docs + round-trip test suite + platform matrix

## Prerequisites

None blocking — feasibility is proven (`P9-001` "SPIKE RESULTS"). Reuses the
reader's companion-discovery, genotype packing, and shard fixtures. Pairs with
the multi-file reader (write sharded → `read_pfile([...])`/`pathmacro:`).

## Branch

`feature/P9-writers` (one branch; phases land as commits, released as v0.8.x).

